_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem statement\r\n\r\nGenerated code includes incorrect pointer operation.\r\n\r\n```go\r\n// GroupPreference group preference\r\n// swagger:model groupPreference\r\ntype GroupPreference map[string]float32\r\n\r\n// Validate validates this group preference\r\nfunc (m GroupPreference) Validate(formats strfmt.Registry) error {\r\n\tvar res []error\r\n\tfor k := range m {\r\n\t\tif swag.IsZero(m[k]) { // not required\r\n\t\t\tcontinue\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif err := validate.Minimum(k, \"body\", float64(*m[k]), -5, false); err != nil {\r\n\t\t\treturn err\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif err := validate.Maximum(k, \"body\", float64(*m[k]), 5, false); err != nil {\r\n\t\t\treturn err\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\tif len(res) > 0 {\r\n\t\treturn errors.CompositeValidationError(res...)\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn nil\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`*m[k]` causes compiler error `invalid indirect of m[k] (type float32)`. It should be `m[k]`\r\n\r\n## Swagger specification\r\n\r\nThe swagger definition is :-\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n  groupPreference:\r\n    type: object\r\n    additionalProperties:\r\n      type: number\r\n      format: float\r\n      minimum: -5\r\n      maximum: 5\r\n    example:\r\n      default: 0\r\n      CN: -0.2\r\n      GB: 0.5\r\n      NL: -5\r\n```\r\n\r\n`format: float` or `format: double`, both have the same issue.\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nswagger generate client -f spec_containing_definition.yaml -t $GOPATH/github.com/user/repo\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\nswagger version: 0.14.0  \r\ngo version: go version go1.10 linux/amd64\r\nOS:  Linux 4.13.0-41-generic #46-Ubuntu SMP\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"casualjim","id":456109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjEwOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/456109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim","html_url":"https://github.com/casualjim","fo